{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review_evidence

    What the applicant sent: the comment as a quotation and the submitted details as tiles, each
    only when present, or one muted line when there is nothing to show this reader. The blocks are
    siblings of the left column's other blocks, which is what spaces them.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * commentlabel string - label of the applicant's comment, plain spelling
    * hascomment boolean - whether the applicant wrote one
    * comment string - what the applicant wrote, ALREADY escaped and with its line breaks
      converted by format_text(FORMAT_PLAIN), which is why it is triple stashed
    * hassnapshot boolean - whether the applicant submitted any detail this reader may see
    * snapshotlabel string - heading of the submitted details
    * snapshotcount string - "X of Y filled in", counted over the rows this reader sees
    * hassnapshotrequired boolean, snapshotrequired string - how many of those are required
    * requiredmark string - the visually hidden "(required)" after a required field's label:
      the outline alone never says it
    * emptyvalue string - what an empty field says
    * snapshot array - one tile per submitted field the reader may see, each with the label and
      the value as they were submitted, both the PLAIN spelling and output through double
      stashes, isempty and isrequired. A value can hold newlines, because a textarea custom field
      is offerable, so the tile carries the same white-space rule the report's own free-text
      cells do
    * hasnothing boolean, nothingsent string - the one line shown when there is neither

    Example context (json):
    {
        "commentlabel": "Comment",
        "hascomment": true,
        "comment": "I would like to join this course.",
        "hassnapshot": true,
        "snapshotlabel": "Submitted details",
        "snapshotcount": "1 of 2 filled in",
        "hassnapshotrequired": true,
        "snapshotrequired": "1 required",
        "requiredmark": "(required)",
        "emptyvalue": "Not filled in",
        "snapshot": [
            {"label": "City/town", "value": "Ouro Preto", "isempty": false, "isrequired": true},
            {"label": "Preferred shift", "value": "", "isempty": true, "isrequired": false}
        ],
        "hasnothing": false,
        "nothingsent": "No comment or submitted details to show."
    }
}}
{{#hascomment}}
    <section class="enrol_apply-reviewcomment" aria-labelledby="enrol_apply_review_comment">
        <h2 class="enrol_apply-blocktitle" id="enrol_apply_review_comment">{{commentlabel}}</h2>
        <blockquote class="enrol_apply-quote mb-0">
            {{#pix}}e/toggle_blockquote, core{{/pix}}
            <div class="enrol_apply-quotetext">{{{comment}}}</div>
        </blockquote>
    </section>
{{/hascomment}}
{{#hassnapshot}}
    {{!
        renderer_test scopes its snapshot assertions to this list, because the page shows
        identifying values elsewhere (the applicant's card). It extracts the list with a non-greedy
        match up to the first closing dl tag, so keep the enrol_apply-snapshot class on the dl and
        nest no dl inside it.
    }}
    <section class="enrol_apply-reviewdetails" aria-labelledby="enrol_apply_review_details">
        <div class="enrol_apply-blockhead">
            <h2 class="enrol_apply-blocktitle" id="enrol_apply_review_details">{{snapshotlabel}}</h2>
            <span class="enrol_apply-blockcount">{{snapshotcount}}{{#hassnapshotrequired}} · <span class="enrol_apply-requiredcount">{{snapshotrequired}}</span>{{/hassnapshotrequired}}</span>
        </div>
        <dl class="enrol_apply-snapshot enrol_apply-tiles mb-0">
            {{#snapshot}}
                <div class="enrol_apply-tile-detail{{#isempty}} enrol_apply-tile-empty{{/isempty}}{{#isrequired}} enrol_apply-tile-required{{/isrequired}}">
                    <dt>{{label}}{{#isrequired}}<span class="visually-hidden"> {{requiredmark}}</span>{{/isrequired}}</dt>
                    <dd class="enrol_apply-linebreaks">{{#isempty}}<span class="enrol_apply-emptyvalue">{{emptyvalue}}</span>{{/isempty}}{{^isempty}}{{value}}{{/isempty}}</dd>
                </div>
            {{/snapshot}}
        </dl>
    </section>
{{/hassnapshot}}
{{#hasnothing}}
    <p class="enrol_apply-nothing">{{#pix}}i/info, core{{/pix}}<span>{{nothingsent}}</span></p>
{{/hasnothing}}
